nodecode-t3 is a rewrite of thetasigmaio's thetasigmaio/hermes-t3-control:
https://github.com/thetasigmaio/hermes-t3-control
commit aeb5493e30e744b414cbfe88a70adb1acd59a1c8
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Jakub Sladek (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the eleven tools of the original, over the same local T3 Code
orchestration API -- the thread list (t3_threads), one thread with its
messages and plan (t3_thread_read), a new thread (t3_thread_create), one
user turn (t3_thread_send), an interrupt (t3_turn_interrupt) and a session
stop (t3_session_stop) -- in Common Lisp: the section and its readers, the
route allowlist, the bearer header, the dispatch commands and their RFC 3339
timestamps and command ids, and the rendering of what T3 answers. The
operator's way in is /t3.

Left out: local-cli authentication (the original mints a five-minute token
by running the T3 CLI and pinning its process through /proc and pidfd; a cell
takes the token the operator already has, from the section or from
T3_ORCHESTRATION_TOKEN) and the opt-in continuation observer with its SQLite
ledger, which needs a patch to the host it ran on. Also left out are four
narrower mutations of the original: setting a thread's mode, implementing a
stored plan, answering a pending approval or question, and settling a
thread; and its long-poll wait. Each is one more dispatch command over the
same route, and none was needed for the lifecycle the cell carries.
